research/audit/wave6-real-analysis-limits.provenance.jsonl-35-{"id":"thm-open-set-algebra-r","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter Proposition 5.4 states arbitrary unions and finite intersections of open subsets of R are open, and gives the corresponding closed-set laws. The local item packages all four clauses and explicitly avoids an empty-intersection convention for the arbitrary closed family; its proof is independently numbered.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave6-real-analysis-limits.provenance.jsonl-36-{"id":"def-interior-closure-boundary-r","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter gives the standard interior, closure, boundary and exterior neighborhood definitions. The local presentation packages the equivalent formulas and R-specific notation in one definition.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
