research/audit/wave6-real-analysis-limits.provenance.jsonl-40-{"id":"thm-open-subsets-of-r-structure","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter states that every open subset of R is a countable union of disjoint open intervals. The local statement identifies those intervals canonically as order components and permits an at-most-countable family, an equivalent convention including the empty set.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
