-- **Index range.** The classical statement writes $x_k = 1/k$ and $y_k = ck$,
-  which requires $k \ge 1$. Written on $\mathbb{N}$, which contains $0$
-  ([[def-sequence]]), the same sequences are $1/(k+1)$ and $c(k+1)$, as above.
